      "summary": {
        "headline": "Correspondence: long-term change in the published values, FY2000 to FY2025.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "Correspondence per household (pieces per household per year) went from 135.1 in FY2014 to 98.6 in FY2025: it fell by 36.5 (27.0%) over the period. Since FY2020 (five years earlier) it fell by 26.5 (21.2%). Since FY2015 (ten years earlier) it fell by 43.8 (30.8%).",
            "metric": "correspondence-per-household",
            "years": [
              2014,
              2025,
              2020,
              2015
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Correspondence mail received per household (pieces per household per year) went from 130.0 in FY2003 to 98.8 in FY2023: it fell by 31.2 (24.0%) over the period. Since FY2018 (five years earlier) it fell by 15.6 (13.6%). Since FY2013 (ten years earlier) it rose by 15.6 (18.7%).",
            "metric": "correspondence-received-per-household",
            "years": [
              2003,
              2023,
              2018,
              2013
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "First-Class correspondence received (millions of pieces) went from 19,470 in FY2000 to 12,864 in FY2023: it fell by 6,606 (33.9%) over the period. Since FY2018 (five years earlier) it fell by 1,911 (12.9%). Since FY2013 (ten years earlier) it fell by 2,633 (17.0%).",
            "metric": "fcm-received-correspondence",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2023,
              2018,
              2013
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Projection, not a published figure: the Linear trend model, fitted on FY2010 to FY2023, puts First-Class correspondence received at 12,113 in FY2028 (80% range 11,509 to 12,717). On past years it beat the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-correspondence",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2028
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "First-Class correspondence sent (millions of pieces) went from 9,512 in FY2000 to 2,305 in FY2023: it fell by 7,207 (75.8%) over the period. Since FY2018 (five years earlier) it fell by 1,136 (33.0%). Since FY2013 (ten years earlier) it fell by 2,611 (53.1%).",
            "metric": "fcm-sent-correspondence",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2023,
              2018,
              2013
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Projection, not a published figure: the Linear trend model, fitted on FY2010 to FY2023, puts First-Class correspondence sent at 1,572 in FY2028 (80% range 983 to 2,162). On past years it beat the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "fcm-sent-correspondence",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2028
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
